# Copy to .env and fill in. Everything here is OPTIONAL - the repo runs without any
# of it, which is deliberate: a submission that only works on the author's laptop is
# worse than one that works everywhere.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a key.


# --- The language model -------------------------------------------------------
# Set it and agent/llm.py calls Anthropic for the rep-facing call briefs, and
# --investigate becomes available. Leave it unset and a documented stand-in writes
# the briefs instead; the run record tags which path ran (cost.mocked, cost.model).
#
# Cost of a full run with a key: about $0.02 for 16 briefs on a small model.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# --- Tracing (optional, and genuinely zero code) -------------------------------
# LangGraph emits to LangSmith natively, so these four variables are the entire
# integration. Every node becomes a span with timings, and every model call carries
# its real token counts.
#
# What a traced run looks like:
#     chain  publish              15ms
#     chain  verify_briefs         5ms
#     llm    ChatAnthropic      2566ms | 687 tokens
#     llm    ChatAnthropic      2134ms | 700 tokens      ... x16
#
# Worth saying plainly: tracing is for debugging the LLM layer, not for the
# business question. "Did the accounts we queued in August beat the ones we held
# back?" is a join against outputs/decisions.csv and the CRM, 90 days later - no
# tracing tool stores that. And a trace cannot stop a bad batch: monitoring/checks.py
# runs before anything publishes, which is where the value is.
LANGSMITH_TRACING=
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
LANGSMITH_PROJECT=
LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com
